// Original C++ AGG 2.6 port of the canvas_ity microbenchmark suite.
// The workloads, their RNG streams, scene geometry, and the timing
// methodology (best trial time on a fresh canvas, repeated) match
// bench/microbench.cpp. Rendering-model differences are listed below.
//
// API-mapping notes and caveats:
// - AGG 2.6 is immediate-mode like canvas_ity, so most workloads map
//   one-to-one. Full circles use the same 16 cubic segments generated by
//   canvas_ity's arc implementation.
// - gradient_linear/radial use AGG's span gradients (span_gradient +
//   gradient_linear/gradient_radial + span_interpolator_linear).  AGG
//   blends in 8-bit sRGB without canvas_ity's gamma linearization. Its
//   focused-radial model also cannot represent a nonzero start radius.
// - composite_ops maps the eleven canvas operations onto AGG's
//   comp_op_rgba_* set through pixfmt_custom_blend_rgba.
// - pattern_tiled, image_scaled, clip_heavy (rect clipping only), and
//   shadow_blurred are omitted (no equivalents; image span filters
//   exist but are a separate pipeline).
// - The fill rule is nonzero, matching canvas_ity's default.
//
//   clang++ -O2 -I<agg>/include -o microbench_agg26 \
//       microbench_agg26.cpp <agg>/src/*.cpp
//
//   ./microbench_agg26 [trials]

#include <agg_rendering_buffer.h>
#include <agg_pixfmt_rgba.h>
